  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of State obligated $81.7M in FY2027 to date. The Department of State recorded 1,253 awards at an average award size of $65.2K. Obligations fell 99.2% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years. Historical annual obligations show $12B in FY22, $11.7B in FY23, $11.7B in FY24, $9.8B in FY25, and $9.7B in FY26. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The FY2027 to date picture is concentrated: the largest category is Security Guards and Patrol Services at $22.7M, and the top vendor is PUTZ SECURITY AG at $6.2M. This snapshot highlights a much smaller fiscal-year-to-date spend compared with multi-billion-dollar totals in recent full fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has State's contract spending changed since prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of State obligated $81.7M in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 99.2% year over year. Annual obligations were $12B in FY22, $11.7B in FY23, $11.7B in FY24, $9.8B in FY25, and $9.7B in FY26. The current fiscal-year-to-date total is a small fraction of those full-year totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are State's top procurement categories and vendors in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest category at $22.7M, followed by Facilities Support Services at $11.9M and Automobile and Light Duty Motor Vehicle Manufacturing at $5M. PUTZ SECURITY AG is the largest vendor at $6.2M, followed by MISCELLANEOUS FOREIGN AWARDEES at $5.9M and ARK GROUP DMCC at $5.8M. The top ten categories and top ten vendors together account for the bulk of the FY2027 to date obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of State spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of State spent $81.7M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of State issued 1,253 awards at an average award size of $65.2K. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does State buy?",
      "a": "State buys Security Guards and Patrol Services, Facilities Support Services, and a mix of transportation and support services led by Security Guards and Patrol Services at $22.7M and Facilities Support Services at $11.9M. Other notable categories include Automobile and Light Duty Motor Vehicle Manufacturing at $5M and Couriers and Express Delivery Services at $4.6M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are State's largest contractors?",
      "a": "PUTZ SECURITY AG is the largest contractor at $6.2M. MISCELLANEOUS FOREIGN AWARDEES is next at $5.9M, followed by ARK GROUP DMCC at $5.8M, KBR SERVICES, LLC at $5.2M, and SENECA STRATEGIC PARTNERS, LLC at $4.9M."
